  "worked_solution": "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$K$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to matrix addition and scalar multiplication) because **the $2\\times 1$  zero matrix does not belong to $K.$** *  \n\nIndeed, adding the entries of the $2\\times 1$  zero matrix yields $0+0=0\\ne 1.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- addition of matrices is associative. $\\,\u2713$\n\n- addition and scalar multiplication of matrices  satisfy the distributive laws. $\u2713$\n\n- Addition of matrices  is commutative. $\\,\u2713$\n\n- $1\\cdot A=A$ for all $A\\in K.$ $\\,\u2713$",
